WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.600
Your skin is peeling…

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:02.950
Does that mean it's working?

3
00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:04.150
RETINOL. AHA · BHA. TONER.

4
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.950
More exfoliants, more results?
Glycolic. Salicylic.

5
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:06.950
MORE IRRITATION.
NOT MORE PROGRESS.

6
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.950
FDA · 21 CFR 333.350

7
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.550
Peeling is a side effect —
not a scorecard.

8
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.550
In trials, more irritation
didn't mean better results.

9
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:13.950
Arch Dermatol · 1995

10
00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:14.950
WHERE'S THE LINE?

11
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.880
NORMAL: Temporary dryness can happen.
(Cutis · 2010)

12
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.900
STOP: Severe burning or swelling?
Stop and ask a doctor. [wall crumbles]

13
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:20.850
THE RESET

14
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.680
Start slowly. Follow directions.
Protect the barrier.

15
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:23.580
One active. Moisturizer. Daytime SPF.

16
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.900
(Cutis · 2006 · FDA guidance · 2005)

17
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:26.880
[chime] 습 SeoulHabit

18
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:27.280
One claim.

19
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:27.880
One boundary.

20
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:28.480
SeoulHabit.

21
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.950
Peeling? Drop to one active
for two weeks.

